            "description": "As a platform operator, I want shared synchronization to process each enabled season independently, so that all competitions remain current without duplicated tenant-level provider calls.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**\n1  With three enabled seasons, GetFixtures, GetTeams, GetStages, GetTournamentGroups and GetStandings use the correct season identifier for each call.\n2  If one season fails, retain its last successful data, record the failure and continue other seasons. Do not delete data because of a failure or incomplete response.\n3  On job retry or concurrent instances, locking prevents overlapping logical work and upserts remain idempotent. Logs include SeasonId, Provider and CorrelationId.\n4  When a season ends and is archived, stop recurring synchronization but retain its data. LiveScores remain shared; FixtureDetail is retrieved by external fixture identifier.\n\nRequired Changes  Update SportMonksOptions, IMatchDataProvider, SportMonksMatchDataProvider, MatchDataSyncJob and FixtureDetailSyncJob. Resolve livescore fixture IDs against the catalog before updating them.\n\nDependencies  BE01 and BE02.",
