            "description": "As a platform operator, I want all seasons to share the provider account budget and expose sync health, so that concurrent tournaments do not exhaust provider limits or hide stale data.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**\n1  When two seasons request the same requested_entity under one account, reserve capacity from one shared quota; each season must not receive an independent copy of the full limit.\n2  On HTTP 429, honor retry or reset metadata and defer nonessential work with backoff. Prevent rapid retries and manual refresh bypassing the budget.\n3  During concurrent live matches across competitions, avoid season starvation, prioritize live and final-result updates, and expose reasons for deferred standings and catalog work.\n4  Health responses show last successful sync, remaining quota, reset, stale and deferred status per bucket and season. Alert after 90 seconds of live-fixture staleness, identifying any deferral reason.\n\nRequired Changes  Update SportMonksRateLimitBudgetService, distributed reservations and Redis keys. Configure a documented account-level ceiling and expose a lower operational limit when needed.\n\nDependencies  BE03; verify the provider account quota scope in the test environment.",
