            "description": "As a player, I want independent season rankings and deterministic scoring, so that predictions across concurrent competitions do not mix streaks or produce duplicate points.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**\n1  Season rankings use outcomes from that season's fixtures. Overall aggregates only available seasons in the published scope; friends rankings apply the same scope and dense-rank semantics.\n2  A correct Premier League prediction followed by an incorrect La Liga prediction does not affect the Premier League streak under the proposed new-season policy. Equal kickoff times are ordered by a stable fixture identifier.\n3  Finalization, retry and recompute create no duplicate outcomes or awards. Late results deterministically recalculate the same season's sequence without moving points between seasons.\n4  WinnerOnly penalty fixtures retain existing CURRENT, PENALTIES, ExactPenalty and CorrectPenalty rules. Enabling a competition does not retroactively change points or reward balances.\n\nRequired Changes  Update the scoring resolver, streak state, EfCorePredictionOutcomeRepository, leaderboards, friends rankings and reporting. Keep leaderboard aggregates separate from any redeemable reward balance.\n\nDependencies  BE02 and BE06; approve season-specific streaks and historical point preservation.",
